# GMS says this OVERRIDES Vessel of Light, and now something can say so: it
# supersedes it and states the whole of what a Paladin holds rather than the
# difference. Its first level already clears the 2nd job skill's last, so the
# point that buys it is never a point spent going backwards.
#
# Its HP recovery is dropped, as the user asked. GMS holds the damage at 25%
# and the attack at 60 past level 10; the ladder here walks a little past both
# under Combat Orders, which is the price of climbing them at all.
#
# The strikes and the reach are the rest of the skill and the reason SkillBoost
# exists: a strike each to Divine Charge and Blast, and two more enemies for
# Divine Charge by the tenth level -- GMS's ceil(L/5).
#
# Those two carry Divine Charge to seven, past the five its 415x200 box holds.
# That stands: the reach rule floors what a swing states for itself, and a
# book's grant is allowed to lift it.
name: "Greater Vessel of Light"
description:
  "Empowers Vessel of Light to its limit with your mastery. Increases Divine "
  "Charge's max number of targets and the attack count of both Divine Charge "
  "and Blast."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_PALADIN skill_order: 8 }
max_level: 10
exceeds_master_level: true
supersedes_skill_name: "Vessel of Light"
base {
  damage_pct: 0.205
  attack: 51
  damage_taken_pct: 0.10
  status_resistance: 10.0
}
per_level {
  damage_pct: 0.005
  attack: 1
}
boost {
  skill_name: "Divine Charge"
  lines: 1
  max_enemies: 1
  max_enemies_per_level: 0.2
}
boost {
  skill_name: "Blast"
  lines: 1
}
